this software.

Scan Blunder Front is published as free and open source software for the
security community. It is intended for authorized security assessment,
defensive review of systems you own or operate, and education.

1. RESPONSIBILITY RESTS ENTIRELY WITH THE OPERATOR. The person or organization
   who runs this software is solely and fully responsible for how it is used,
   for choosing the targets it is pointed at, and for every consequence that
   follows. The authors and contributors neither control nor supervise any use
   of this software.

2. AUTHORIZATION IS REQUIRED. This software sends requests to systems you
   specify, and in its default configuration those requests are active (for
   example, it probes paths such as /.env and /.git/config). Scanning systems
   without the explicit permission of their owner may be illegal in your
   jurisdiction. Obtain written authorization before scanning anything that is
   not yours.

3. NO LIABILITY FOR MISUSE. The authors and contributors are not responsible
   for any damage, disruption, data loss, service interruption, legal
   consequence, or any other harm arising from the use or misuse of this
   software, whether that use was intentional, negligent, or accidental. This
   includes use against third-party systems, use in production environments,
   and any action taken on the basis of its output.

4. NO GUARANTEE OF CORRECTNESS. The results are produced by heuristics. The
   software may report findings that are not real, and it may fail to report
   real vulnerabilities. Its output is not a certification of security and must
   not be relied upon as one. Verify every finding independently before acting
   on it.

